Subject: [freebsd-ports PATCH] mail/resend-cli: Command line interface for the
 Resend email API
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev

Resend CLI is the official command line interface for Resend, an email
API for developers. It sends and schedules email, and manages domains,
API keys, contacts, segments, broadcasts, templates, and webhooks. It is
built for interactive use as well as for scripts, CI pipelines, and AI
agents, with JSON output for machine consumption.

The npm package ships a self-contained bundle, so the port installs it
as is. Its esbuild dependency is used only to render React Email
templates and is not packaged; pkg-message says so.

WWW: https://resend.com/docs/cli
---
Notes for review:

Version: 2.23.0 is the newest release on npm and GitHub. Later npm
uploads are 2.22.0-preview-inboxes.* pre-releases, and no version is
deprecated.

Mechanism: the published tarball's dist/cli.cjs is an esbuild bundle
that requires only node: builtins, except for esbuild itself (checked
with grep for require calls). So the port follows devel/spago: fetch
the registry tarball and install the bundle, with no node_modules. The
14 ports on Tools/scripts/npmjs-fetch-with-dependencies.sh install a
full dependency tree instead. Here that would duplicate the bundle, and
npm would pull a host-specific @esbuild/<platform> binary into a
NO_ARCH package. The cost is that "--react-email" fails because esbuild
cannot be loaded; pkg-message says so. If that feature is wanted, the
fetch script is the alternative.

Wrapper: bin/resend follows www/immich-cli (SUB_FILES, explicit node).
It defaults RESEND_NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER=1, which is upstream's own knob.
Otherwise the CLI polls the GitHub releases API and tells pkg users to
upgrade from GitHub.

Dependencies: package.json says engines node >=22. USES=nodejs:run
resolves to the default (lts, node24), as in 28 other ports. A user who
sets the default to 20 would get an unsupported Node.

pkg-message: telemetry is on by default (PostHog) with DO_NOT_TRACK or
RESEND_TELEMETRY_DISABLED to opt out. Secure credential storage
supports only darwin, linux, and win32, so FreeBSD falls back to
~/.config/resend/credentials.json. Both were checked in the bundle.

Checked: portclippy, portfmt -D, and portlint -A are clean. makesum
fetched the distfile, and its sha1 matches the registry's shasum.
Not checked: the build, stage, and plist. Node is not installed here,
so the CLI was not run.

